{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>You shall not plow with an ox and a donkey.</b> It is joined with sowing, and HaShem has compassion on all His works, for the strength of the donkey is not like the strength of the ox. And on account of sowing He said kilayim (diverse kinds). He has already mentioned it in general terms, and here He specified that it is wool and linen, not others."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:20.104112746Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}